  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "Top row (y = 0): a 2 mm HeNe beam is expanded 4x by a Keplerian telescope (f = 25 mm and f = 100 mm plano-convex lenses, spaced f1 + f2 = 125 mm, curved faces towards the collimated side) and the 8 mm beam is focused by an f = 100 mm bi-convex lens onto a power meter. Bottom row (y = 150): a wide 40 mm collimated beam through a strongly curved f = 50 mm bi-convex lens shows spherical aberration - marginal rays cross the axis well before the paraxial focus, so the screen at the paraxial focus sees a blur instead of a point.",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Lens Focusing & Spherical Aberration"
  },
